"""Original mixed-length correction and recall trajectories."""
ROWS=[]
def add(family,group,*turns):ROWS.append(dict(family=family,group=group,turns=turns))
add('correction','borrowed_box_relabel',
('I borrowed a storage box from May. I labelled it May’s tools, but it holds my fabric.','The label confuses ownership of the box with its contents. You could write “My fabric — box borrowed from May.”'),
('May has given me the box now.','Then the box is yours too; the borrowed-box note no longer applies.'),
('Suggest a plain label.','Fabric'),
('I added sewing patterns to it as well.','Fabric and sewing patterns'),
('The patterns are borrowed from Len, unlike the box.','You could label it “Fabric and sewing patterns” and keep a separate note that the patterns must go back to Len.'),
('Help me write that separate note.','Return the borrowed sewing patterns to Len.'),
('Do I still owe May the storage box?','No. You said May gave it to you.'),
('Which contents need returning?','The sewing patterns, to Len.'))
add('correction','event_host_multiple_roles',
('Nora is hosting the craft morning, and Leo will demonstrate weaving.','Nora hosts the morning; Leo gives the weaving demonstration.'),
('Leo cannot come. Nora will demonstrate as well as host.','Nora will now both host and demonstrate weaving.'),
('Write a short introduction.','Welcome to our craft morning. Nora will host and demonstrate weaving.'),
('We have not chosen who handles registration.','Leave that role unassigned rather than assuming Nora is doing it too.'),
('Would it be too much to mention all the job changes in the welcome?','The welcome can simply describe the current arrangement. It does not need the history of every change.'),
('Sam has now agreed to handle registration.','Sam handles registration; Nora hosts and demonstrates weaving.'),
('Give me the final role list, without Leo.','Nora: host and weaving demonstration.\nSam: registration.'),
('Did Nora stop hosting when she took on the demonstration?','No. She took on the demonstration in addition to hosting.'))
add('correction','permission_withdraw_one_photo',
('The club may use the group photo and the garden photo in its newsletter.','Both the group photo and garden photo are currently allowed for the newsletter.'),
('I want to withdraw permission for the group photo only.','The garden photo remains allowed. Permission for the group photo is withdrawn.'),
('Write a clear message.','Please do not use the group photo in the newsletter. You may still use the garden photo.'),
('Someone asks if all my photographs are now banned.','No. Your change applies to the group photo; the garden photo remains permitted.'),
('I want to keep the message friendly without weakening the request.','Please leave the group photo out of the newsletter. The garden photo is still fine to use. Thanks for understanding.'),
('We are discussing a printed newsletter, not a website.','The permission discussed here concerns the printed newsletter. It does not establish permission for website use.'),
('Can the garden photo go on the website based on what I said?','That has not been authorised in the information you shared.'))
add('correction','story_weather_local_change',
('In my story, it rains in the morning and clears by evening.','The day starts rainy and becomes clear by evening.'),
('Make the evening foggy instead. Keep the morning rain.','The morning is rainy, and the evening is foggy.'),
('Give me a simple morning sentence.','Rain tapped against the window throughout the morning.'),
('Now one for the evening, without rain.','By evening, fog softened the outline of the trees.'),
('I like the word softened. Could it describe a sound too?','Yes. A sound can be described as softened when it becomes less sharp or intense.'),
('Back to the story: someone suggests a clear sunset. Would that match our current evening?','Not as written. The current evening is foggy, so a clear sunset would need another explicit change.'),
('Which part of the weather plan never changed?','The morning rain.'))
add('correction','archive_date_confidence',
('I labelled a family photo 1984, but that was only my guess.','The label should show that uncertainty, such as “Possibly 1984,” rather than present the year as established.'),
('My aunt has found a dated copy showing 1986.','That gives you a stated source for changing the year to 1986.'),
('Write the label with a short source note.','1986 — date from the copy found by my aunt.'),
('Do not say she took the photo. We do not know who did.','The source note identifies where the date came from, not who took the photograph.'),
('Should I keep 1984 as an equally confirmed date?','No. You described 1984 as a guess and 1986 as supported by the dated copy.'),
('I will keep the old guess in my research notes.','That preserves the history of your research without making the old guess the current caption.'),
('What year belongs on the current label?','1986.'))
add('correction','garden_path_partial_reopen',
('The garden’s north and south paths were closed after maintenance.','Both paths were closed after maintenance.'),
('The notice now says the north path has reopened. The south path remains closed.','The north path is open; the south path is still closed.'),
('Write a visitor update.','The north path has reopened. Please continue to avoid the closed south path.'),
('Can the heading say all paths open?','No. That would wrongly include the south path.'),
('Visitors ask whether the flower beds are open. I have no information about that.','You can say the notice only gives the path status and does not confirm access to the flower beds.'),
('Someone says reopened means everything reopened.','Here, the notice specifically names the north path. That does not extend to the south path or other areas.'),
('Give me just the still-closed path.','The south path.'))
add('correction','music_request_latest_version',
('For my background playlist, include instrumental tracks only. I do not want lyrics while reading.','Keep the playlist instrumental so there are no sung lyrics competing with your reading.'),
('I am done reading now. For dinner, quiet songs with words are fine.','For dinner, quiet songs with lyrics are now acceptable.'),
('Should the playlist still be loud and energetic?','You asked for quiet songs. Finishing the reading task did not introduce a preference for loud music.'),
('Give me a short note describing the dinner playlist, not actual song recommendations.','Quiet songs for dinner; lyrics are welcome.'),
('Tomorrow I will read again and use my original rule for that session.','For tomorrow’s reading, return to instrumental tracks only.'),
('Does tomorrow’s rule change the dinner request we just made?','No. The dinner playlist allows quiet songs with lyrics; the instrumental-only rule applies to the reading session.'),
('Why are the two rules not contradictory?','They apply to different activities: dinner and reading.'))
add('correction','family_message_addressee_fix',
('Draft a note from me to my father saying my sister will visit him on Sunday.','My sister will visit you on Sunday.'),
('Actually the note is for my sister, confirming she will visit Dad.','You will visit Dad on Sunday.'),
('Make it a question checking the plan, not a statement.','Are you still planning to visit Dad on Sunday?'),
('Would “Is Dad visiting you?” mean the same thing?','No. That reverses who is visiting whom.'),
('She replies yes, but Saturday rather than Sunday.','The confirmed plan is that your sister will visit Dad on Saturday.'),
('Now write a message to Dad with that update.','My sister has confirmed she will visit you on Saturday.'),
('Who is travelling, according to the final plan?','Your sister is visiting your father.'))
